Day 1
Java is portable because of JVM
Java is Simple and Secure
JVM used to understand byte code in any Operating System
JVM us platform independent but Java is not
JVM run bytecode in secured environment

Java is used in Backend
Read about servlets and applets


Day 2
JVM : Java Virtual Machine
Java src code convert in byte code using compiler 
To run byte code we need JVM which is different for different platform 
Byte code converted into Machine code using JVM 

JRE : Java Runtime Environment
      JVM + Class libraries(Internal Librairies for printing in console, read and write file)


Java is both compiled and Interpreted Language

Conversion from src code to byte code uses compiler
Conversion from byte code to machine code use interpretor
Nowdays JVM uses interpretor + JIT compiler for conversion

JVM provide security using Sandbox Model(Safe Environment)
JVM provide Garbage Collection 

JDK : Java Developement Kit
JRE + Compiler + Debugger + Java Docs etc...

JSE : Java Standard Edition (Core Java)
JEE : Java Enterprise Edition or Jakarta EE (Webapps and all...) 
JME : Java Micro Edition  
